What is the difference between a function call and a function reference? 
A function call is when you invoke the function, while a function reference is when you refer to the function without calling it. For example, in the following code: 
void my_function() {
   cout << "Hello World"; 
} 
int main() { 
   my_function(); // function call 
   my_function = &my_function; // function reference 
   return 0; 
}assistant

In the above example, my_function() is called when the program reaches the line my_function(); and its value is referenced when my_function = &my_function; is executed. A function reference allows you to pass the function as an argument to another function or store it in a variable, while a function call executes the code within the function.ávajícíuser

